2. Now Lentement, inspirez as much air as possible and then start to expirez as much as possible while bringing your stomach in as much as possible and hold this position. Try to visualize your navel touching your backbone.
3. One isometric contraction is around 20 seconds. During the 20 second hold, try to breathe normally. Then inspirez and bring your stomach back to the position de départ.
4. Once you have practiced cet exercice, try to perform cet exercice for longer than 20 seconds. Conseil : You can work your way up to 40-60 seconds.
5. Répétez for the recommended amount of sets.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Stomach_Vacuum/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Straight-Arm Dumbbell Pullover', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Place a haltère standing up on a flat banc.
2. Ensuring that the haltère stays securely placed at the top of the banc, lie perpendiculaire à the banc (torse across it as in forming a cross) with only your épaules lying on the surface. hanches should be below the banc and legs bent with feet firmly on le sol. The head will be off the banc as well.
3. Grasp the haltère with both hands and hold it straight over your poitrine bras tendus. Both palms should be pressing against the underside one of the sides of the haltère. C''est votre position de départ.
Caution: Always ensure that the haltère used for cet exercice is secure. Using a haltère with loose plates can result in the haltère falling apart and falling on your face.
4. While keeping vos bras straight, lower the poids Lentement, in an arc behind votre tête while breathing in until you feel a stretch on the poitrine.
5. At that point, bring the haltère back to the position de départ using the arc through which the poids was lowered and expirez as you perform this movement.
6. Hold the poids on the initial position for a second and Répétez the motion for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Straight-Arm_Dumbbell_Pullover/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Straight-Arm Pulldown', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. You will start by grabbing the wide bar from the top pulley of a pulldown machine and using a wider than épaule-width pronated (palms down) grip. Step backwards two feet or so.
2. Bend your torse forward at the waist by around 30-degrees with vos bras fully extended in front of you and a slight bend at the coudes. If vos bras are not fully extended then you need to step a bit more backwards until they are. Once vos bras are fully extended and your torse is slightly bent at the waist, tighten the lats and then you are ready to begin.
3. While keeping the arms straight, pull the bar down by contracting the lats until vos mains are next to the side of the cuisses. Expirez as you perform this step.
4. While keeping the arms straight, go back to the position de départ while breathing in.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Straight-Arm_Pulldown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Straight Bar Bench Mid Rows', 'Milieu du dos', 'Barre', '1. Place a loaded barre on the end of a banc. Standing on the banc behind the bar, take a medium, pronated grip. Tenez-vous debout avec your hanches back and poitrine up, maintaining a neutral spine. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Row the bar to your torse by retracting the omoplates and flexing the coudes. Use a controlled movement with no jerking.
3. Après une pause, Lentement, return the bar to the position de départ, ensuring to go all the way down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Straight_Bar_Bench_Mid_Rows/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Straight Raises on Incline Bench', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Place a bar on the ground behind the head of an incline banc.
2. Lay on the banc face down. With a pronated grip, pick the barre up from le sol, keeping vos bras straight. Allow the bar to hang straight down. C''est votre position de départ.
3. To begin, raise the barre out in front of votre tête while keeping vos bras extended.
4. Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Straight_Raises_on_Incline_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Stride Jump Crossover', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Stand to the side of a box with your inside foot on top of it, close to the edge.
2. Begin by swinging the arms upward as you push through the top leg, jumping upward as high as possible. Attempt to drive the opposite genou upward.
3. Land in the opposite position that you started, on the opposite side of the box. The foot that was initially on the box will now be on the ground, with the opposite foot now on the box.
4. Répétez le mouvement, crossing back over to the other side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Stride_Jump_Crossover/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sumo Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a bar loaded on the ground. Approach the bar so that the bar intersects the middle of the feet. The feet should be set very wide, near the collars. Bend at the hanches to grip the bar. The arms should be directly below the épaules, inside the legs, and you can use a pronated grip, a mixed grip, or hook grip. Relax the épaules, which in effect lengthens vos bras.
2. Take a breath, and then lower your hanches, looking forward with votre tête with your poitrine up. Drive through le sol, spreading vos pieds apart, with your poids on the back half of vos pieds. Extend through the hanches and genous.
3. As the bar passes through the genous, lean back and drive the hanches into the bar, pulling your omoplates together.
4. Return the poids to the ground by bending at the hanches and controlling the poids on the way down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sumo_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sumo Deadlift with Bands', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. To deadlift with short bands, simply loop them over the bar before you start, and step into them to set up. Ensure that they under the back half of your foot, directly where you are driving into le sol.
2. Begin with a bar loaded on the ground. Approach the bar so that the bar intersects the middle of the feet. The feet should be set very wide, near the collars. Bend at the hanches to grip the bar. The arms should be directly below the épaules, inside the legs, and you can use a pronated grip, a mixed grip, or hook grip.
3. Take a breath, and then lower your hanches, looking forward with votre tête with your poitrine up. Drive through le sol, spreading vos pieds apart, with your poids on the back half of vos pieds. Extend through the hanches and genous.
4. As the bar passes through the genous, lean back and drive the hanches into the bar, pulling your omoplates together.
5. Return the poids to the ground by bending at the hanches and controlling the poids on the way down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sumo_Deadlift_with_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sumo Deadlift with Chains', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. You can attach the chains to the sleeves of the bar, or just drape the middle over the bar so there is a greater poids increase as you lift. Attempt to keep the ends of the chains away from the plates so you don''t hit them when you lower the poids.
2. Begin with a bar loaded on the ground. Approach the bar so that the bar intersects the middle of the feet. The feet should be set very wide, near the collars. Bend at the hanches to grip the bar. The arms should be directly below the épaules, inside the legs, and you can use a pronated grip, a mixed grip, or hook grip. Relax the épaules, which in effect lengthens vos bras.
3. Take a breath, and then lower your hanches, looking forward with votre tête with your poitrine up. Drive through le sol, spreading vos pieds apart, with your poids on the back half of vos pieds. Extend through the hanches and genous.
4. As the bar passes through the genous, lean back and drive the hanches into the bar, pulling your omoplates together.
5. Return the poids to the ground by bending at the hanches and controlling the poids on the way down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sumo_Deadlift_with_Chains/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Superman', 'Bas du dos', 'Poids de corps', '1. To begin, lie straight and face down on le sol or exercise mat. vos bras should be fully extended in front of you. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Simultaneously raise vos bras, legs, and poitrine off of le sol and hold this contraction for 2 seconds. Conseil : Squeeze your lower back to get the best results from cet exercice. Remember to expirez during this movement. Note: When holding the contracted position, you should look like superman when he is flying.
3. Lentement, begin to lower vos bras, legs and poitrine back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. prescribed in your program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Superman/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Supine Chest Throw', 'Triceps', 'Medecine ball', '1. This drill is great for poitrine passes when you lack a partner or a wall of sufficient strength. Lay on the ground on votre dos with your genous bent.
2. Begin with the ball on your poitrine, held with both hands on the bottom.
3. Explode up, extending through the coude to throw the ball directly above you as high as possible.
4. Catch the ball with both hands as it comes down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Supine_Chest_Throw/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Supine One-Arm Overhead Throw', 'Abdominaux', 'Medecine ball', '1. Lay on the ground on votre dos with your genous bent. Hold the ball with one hand, extending the arm fully behind votre tête. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Initiate le mouvement at the épaule, throwing the ball directly forward of you as you sit up, attempting to go for maximum distance.
3. The ball can be thrown to a partner or bounced off of a wall.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Supine_One-Arm_Overhead_Throw/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Supine Two-Arm Overhead Throw', 'Abdominaux', 'Medecine ball', '1. Lay on the ground on votre dos with your genous bent.
2. Hold the ball with both hands, extending the arms fully behind votre tête. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Initiate le mouvement at the épaule, throwing the ball directly forward of you as you sit up, attempting to go for maximum distance.
4. The ball can be thrown to a partner or bounced off of a wall.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Supine_Two-Arm_Overhead_Throw/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Suspended Fallout', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Adjust the straps so the handles are at an appropriate height, below waist level.
2. Begin standing and grasping the handles. Lean into the straps, moving to an incline push-up position. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping vos bras straight, lean further into the suspension straps, bringing votre corps closer to the ground, allowing your épaules to extend, raising vos bras up and over votre tête.
4. Maintain a neutral spine and keep the rest of votre corps straight, your épaules being the only joints allowed to move.
5. Pause during the peak contraction, and then Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Bas du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Suspended_Fallout/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Suspended Push-Up', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Anchor your suspension straps securely to the top of a rack or other object.
2. Leaning into the straps, take a handle in each hand and move into a push-up plank position. You should be as close to parallel to the ground as you can manage with vos bras fully extended, maintaining good posture.
3. Maintaining a straight, rigid torse, descend Lentement, by allowing the coudes to flex.
4. Continue until your coudes break 90 degrees, pausing before you extend to Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Suspended_Push-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Suspended Reverse Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Secure a set of suspension straps with the handles hanging about a foot off of the ground. Move yourself into a pushup plank position facing away from the rack.
2. Place vos pieds into the handles. You should maintain a straight posture, not allowing the hanches to sag. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin le mouvement by flexing the genous and hanches, drawing the genous to your torse. As you do so, anteriorly tilt your pelvis, allowing your spine to flex.
4. At the top of the controlled motion, Revenez en position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Suspended_Reverse_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Suspended Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Autre', '1. Suspend your straps at around poitrine height. Take a handle in each hand and lean back. Keep votre corps erect and votre tête and poitrine up. vos bras should be fully extended. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by flexing the coude to initiate le mouvement. Protract your omoplates as you do so.
3. At the completion of the motion pause, and then Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Suspended_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Suspended Split Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Suspend your straps so the handles are 18-30 inches from le sol.
2. Facing away from the setup, place your rear foot into the handle behind you. Keep votre tête looking forward and your poitrine up, with your genou slightly bent. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Descend by flexing the genou and hanches, lowering yourself to the ground. Keep your poids on the heel of your foot and maintain your posture throughout the exercise.
4. At the bottom of le mouvement, reverse the motion, extending through the hanche and genou to Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Suspended_Split_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Svend Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Begin in a standing position.
2. Press two lightweight plates together with vos mains. Hold the plates together close to your poitrine to create an isometric contraction in your poitrine muscles. Your fingers should be pointed forward. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Squeeze the plates between your palms and extend vos bras directly out in front of you in a controlled motion.
4. Pause at the top of the motion, and then Lentement, Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Svend_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('T-Bar Row with Handle', 'Milieu du dos', 'Barre', '1. Position a bar into a landmine or in a corner to keep it from moving. Load an appropriate poids onto your end.
2. Stand over the bar, and position a Double D row handle around the bar next to the collar. Using your hanches and legs, rise to a standing position.
3. Assume a wide stance with your hanches back and your poitrine up. vos bras should be extended. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Pull the poids to your upper abdomen by retracting the omoplates and flexing the coudes. Do not jerk the poids or cheat during le mouvement.
5. Après une pause, Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/T-Bar_Row_with_Handle/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Tate Press', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat with a haltère in each hand on top of your cuisses. The palms of your hand will be facing each other.
2. By using your cuisses to help you get the haltères up, clean the haltères one arm at a time so that you can hold them in front of you at épaule width. Note: when holding the haltères in front of you, make sure vos bras are wider than épaule width apart from each other using a pronated (palms forward) grip. Allow your coudes to point out. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping the upper arms stationary, Lentement, move the haltères in and down in a semi circular motion until they touch the upper poitrine while inhaling. Keep full control of the haltères en permanence and do not move the upper arms nor rest the haltères on the poitrine.
4. As you Expirez, move the haltères up using your triceps and the same semi-circular motion but in reverse. Attempt to keep the haltères together as they move up. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down again Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.
5. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Tate_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('The Straddle', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Begin in a seated, upright position. Start by extending vos jambes in front of you in a V.
2. With vos mains on le sol, lean forward as far as possible. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Mollets. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/The_Straddle/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Thigh Abductor', 'Abducteurs', 'Machine', '1. To begin, sit down on the abductor machine and select a poids you are comfortable with. When vos jambes are positioned properly, grip the handles on each side. Your entire upper body (from the waist up) should be stationary. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Lentement, press against the machine with vos jambes to move them away from each other while exhaling.
3. Feel the contraction for a second and begin to move vos jambes back to the position de départ while breathing in. Note: Remember to keep your upper body stationary to prevent any injuries from occurring.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Thigh_Abductor/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Thigh Adductor', 'Adducteurs', 'Machine', '1. To begin, sit down on the adductor machine and select a poids you are comfortable with. When vos jambes are positioned properly on the leg pads of the machine, grip the handles on each side. Your entire upper body (from the waist up) should be stationary. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Lentement, press against the machine with vos jambes to move them towards each other while exhaling.
3. Feel the contraction for a second and begin to move vos jambes back to the position de départ while breathing in. Note: Remember to keep your upper body stationary and avoid fast jerking motions in order to prevent any injuries from occurring.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Thigh_Adductor/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Tire Flip', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Begin by gripping the bottom of the tire on the tread, and position vos pieds back a bit. Your poitrine should be driving into the tire.
2. To lift the tire, extend through the hanches, genous, and chevilles, driving into the tire and up.
3. As the tire reaches a angle de 45 degrés, step forward and drive a genou into the tire. As you do so adjust your grip to the upper portion of the tire and push it forward as hard as possible to complete the turn. Répétez as necessary.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Pectoraux, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Tire_Flip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Toe Touchers', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. To begin, Allongez-vous au sol or an exercise mat with votre dos pressed against le sol. vos bras should be lying across your sides with the paumes vers down.
2. vos jambes should be touching each other. Lentement, elevate vos jambes up in the air until they are almost perpendiculaire à le sol with a slight bend at the genous. vos pieds should be parallèle au sol.
3. Move vos bras so that they are fully extended at a angle de 45 degrés from le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
4. While keeping your lower back pressed against le sol, Lentement, lift your torse and use vos mains to try and touch your toes. Remember to expirez while perform this part of the exercise.
5. Lentement, begin to lower your torse and arms back down to the position de départ while inhaling. Remember to keep vos bras straight out pointing towards your toes.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Toe_Touchers/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Torso Rotation', 'Abdominaux', 'Swiss ball', '1. Levez-vousright holding an exercise ball with both hands. Extend vos bras so the ball is straight out in front of you. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Rotate your torse to one side, keeping your eyes on the ball as you move. Now, rotate back to the opposite direction. Répétez for 10-20 repetitions.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Torso_Rotation/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Trail Running/Walking', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Running or hiking on trails will get the blood pumping and heart beating almost immediately. Make sure you have good shoes. While you use the muscles in your mollets and buttocks to pull yourself up a hill, the genous, joints and chevilles absorb the bulk of the pounding coming back down. Take smaller steps as you walk downhill, keep your genous bent to reduce the impact and slow down to avoid falling.
2. A 150 lb person can burn over 200 calories for 30 minutes walking uphill, compared to 175 on a flat surface. If running the trail, a 150 lb person can burn well over 500 calories in 30 minutes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Trail_Running_Walking/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Trap Bar Deadlift', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. For cet exercice load a trap bar, also known as a hex bar, to an appropriate poids resting on the ground. Stand in the center of the apparatus and grasp both handles.
2. Lower your hanches, look forward with votre tête and keep your poitrine up.
3. Begin le mouvement by driving through the heels and extend your hanches and genous. Avoid rounding votre dos en permanence.
4. At the completion of le mouvement, lower the poids back to the ground under control.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Trap_Bar_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Tricep Dumbbell Kickback', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Start with a haltère in each hand and your paumes vers your torse. Keep votre dos straight with a slight bend in the genous and bend forward at the waist. Your torse should be almost parallèle au sol. Make sure to keep votre tête up. Your upper arms should be close to your torse and parallèle au sol. Your forearms should be pointed towards le sol as you hold the poids. There should be a angle de 90 degrés formed between your forearm and upper arm. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Now, while keeping your upper arms stationary, expirez and use your triceps to lift the poids until the arm is fully extended. Focus on moving the forearm.
3. Après une pause, at the top contraction, inspirez and Lentement, lower the haltères back down to the position de départ.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Tricep_Dumbbell_Kickback/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Tricep Side Stretch', 'Triceps', 'Autre', '1. Bring right arm across votre corps and over your left épaule, holding your coude with your left hand, until you feel a stretch in your triceps. Then Répétez for your other arm.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Tricep_Side_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Triceps Overhead Extension with Rope', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a rope to a low pulley. After selecting an appropriate poids, grasp the rope with both hands and face away from the cable.
2. Position vos mains behind votre tête with your coudes point straight up. Your coudes should start out flexed, and you can stagger your stance and lean gently away from the machine to create greater stability. C''est votre position de départ.
3. To perform le mouvement, extend through the coude while keeping the upper arm in position, raising vos mains above votre tête.
4. Squeeze your triceps at the top of le mouvement, and Lentement, lower the poids back to the start position.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Triceps_Overhead_Extension_with_Rope/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Triceps Pushdown', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a straight or angled bar to a high pulley and grab with an prise en pronation (paumes vers down) at épaule width.
2. Standing upright with the torse straight and a very small inclination forward, bring the upper arms close to votre corps and perpendiculaire à le sol. The forearms should be pointing up towards the pulley as they hold the bar. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Using the triceps, bring the bar down until it touches the front of your cuisses and the arms are fully extended perpendiculaire à le sol. The upper arms should always remain stationary next to your torse and only the forearms should move. Expirez as you perform this movement.
4. After a second hold at the contracted position, bring the bar Lentement, up to the starting point. Inspirez as you perform this step.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Triceps_Pushdown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Triceps Pushdown - Rope Attachment', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a rope attachment to a high pulley and grab with a neutral grip (paumes vers each other).
2. Standing upright with the torse straight and a very small inclination forward, bring the upper arms close to votre corps and perpendiculaire à le sol. The forearms should be pointing up towards the pulley as they hold the rope with the paumes vers each other. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Using the triceps, bring the rope down as you bring each side of the rope to the side of your cuisses. At the end of le mouvement the arms are fully extended and perpendiculaire à le sol. The upper arms should always remain stationary next to your torse and only the forearms should move. Expirez as you perform this movement.
4. After holding for a second, at the contracted position, bring the rope Lentement, up to the starting point. Inspirez as you perform this step.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Triceps_Pushdown_-_Rope_Attachment/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Triceps Pushdown - V-Bar Attachment', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a V-Bar to a high pulley and grab with an prise en pronation (paumes vers down) at épaule width.
2. Standing upright with the torse straight and a very small inclination forward, bring the upper arms close to votre corps and perpendiculaire à le sol. The forearms should be pointing up towards the pulley as they hold the bar. The thumbs should be higher than the small finger. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Using the triceps, bring the bar down until it touches the front of your cuisses and the arms are fully extended perpendiculaire à le sol. The upper arms should always remain stationary next to your torse and only the forearms should move. Expirez as you perform this movement.
4. After a second hold at the contracted position, bring the V-Bar Lentement, up to the starting point. Inspirez as you perform this step.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Triceps_Pushdown_-_V-Bar_Attachment/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Triceps Stretch', 'Triceps', 'Autre', '1. Reach your hand behind votre tête, grasp your coude and gently pull. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds, then switch sides.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Triceps_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Tuck Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. To begin, Allongez-vous au sol or an exercise mat with votre dos pressed against le sol. vos bras should be lying across your sides with the paumes vers down.
2. vos jambes should be crossed by wrapping one cheville around the other. Lentement, elevate vos jambes up in the air until your cuisses are perpendiculaire à le sol with a slight bend at the genous. Note: Your genous and toes should be parallèle au sol as opposed to the cuisses.
3. Move vos bras from le sol and cross them so they are resting on your poitrine. C''est votre position de départ.
4. While keeping your lower back pressed against le sol, Lentement, lift your torse. Remember to expirez while perform this part of the exercise.
5. Lentement, begin to lower your torse back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Tuck_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Two-Arm Dumbbell Preacher Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a haltère with each arm and place the upper arms on top of the preacher banc or the incline banc. The haltère should be held at épaule length. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you Inspirez, Lentement, lower the haltères until your upper arm is extended and the biceps is fully stretched.
3. As you expirez, use the biceps to curl the poids up until your biceps is entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule height.
4. Squeeze the biceps hard for a second at the contracted position and Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Dumbbell_Preacher_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Two-Arm Kettlebell Clean', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place two kettlebells between vos pieds. To get in the position de départ, push your butt back and look straight ahead.
2. Clean the kettlebells to your épaules by extending through the legs and hanches as you raise the kettlebells towards your épaules. Rotate your poignets as you do so.
3. Lower the kettlebells back to the position de départ and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Kettlebell_Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Two-Arm Kettlebell Jerk', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Clean two kettlebells to your épaules. Clean the kettlebells to your épaules by extending through the legs and hanches as you swing the kettlebells towards your épaules. Rotate your poignets as you do so, so that the palms face forward. Squat down a few inches and reverse the motion rapidly driving both kettlebells overhead. Immediately after the initial push, squat down again and get under the kettlebells. Once the kettlebells are locked out, Levez-vousright to complete the exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Quadriceps, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Kettlebell_Jerk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Two-Arm Kettlebell Military Press', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Clean two kettlebells to your épaules. Clean the kettlebells to your épaules by extending through the legs and hanches as you swing the kettlebells towards your épaules. Rotate your poignets as you do so, so that the palms face forward.
2. Press the kettlebells up and out. As the kettlebells pass votre tête, lean into the poids so that the kettlebells are racked behind votre tête. Make sure to contract your lats, butt, and stomach for added stability.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Kettlebell_Military_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Two-Arm Kettlebell Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place two kettlebells in front of vos pieds. Bend your genous slightly and then push your butt out as much as possible as you bend over to get in the position de départ.
2. Grab both kettlebells and pull them to your stomach, retracting your omoplates and flexing the coudes. Keep votre dos straight. Lower and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Kettlebell_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Underhand Cable Pulldowns', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Sit down on a pull-down machine with a wide bar attached to the top pulley. Adjust the genou pad of the machine to fit your height. These pads will prevent votre corps from being raised by the resistance attached to the bar.
2. Grab the pull-down bar with the paumes vers your torse (a supinated grip). Make sure that the hands are placed closer than the épaule width.
3. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip width, bring your torse back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. C''est votre position de départ.
4. As you Expirez, pull the bar down until it touches your upper poitrine by drawing the épaules and the upper arms down and back. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the entièrement contracté position and keep the coudes close to votre corps. The upper torse should remain stationary as your bring the bar to you and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar.
5. After a second on the contracted position, while breathing in, Lentement, bring the bar back to the position de départ when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched.
6. Répétez this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Underhand_Cable_Pulldowns/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Upper Back-Leg Grab', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. While seated, bend forward to hug your cuisses from underneath with both arms.
2. Keep your genous together and vos jambes extended out as you bring your poitrine down to your genous. You can also stretch your middle back by pulling votre dos away from your genous as your hugging them.', 'Muscles secondaires : Bas du dos, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Upper_Back-Leg_Grab/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Upper Back Stretch', 'Milieu du dos', 'Autre', '1. Clasp fingers together with your thumbs pointing down, round your épaules as you reach vos mains forward.', 'Muscles secondaires : Milieu du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Upper_Back_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Upright Barbell Row', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Grasp a barre with an prise en pronation that is slightly less than épaule width. The bar should be resting on the top of your cuisses with vos bras extended and a slight bend in your coudes. votre dos should also be straight. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Now expirez and use the sides of your épaules to lift the bar, raising your coudes up and to the side. Keep the bar close to votre corps as you raise it. Continue to lift the bar until it nearly touches your chin. Conseil : Your coudes should drive the motion, and should always be higher than your forearms. Remember to keep your torse stationary and pause for a second at the top of le mouvement.
3. Lower the bar back down Lentement, to the position de départ. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Upright_Barbell_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Upright Cable Row', 'Trapèzes', 'Poulie', '1. Grasp a straight bar cable attachment that is attached to a low pulley with a pronated (paumes vers your cuisses) grip that is slightly less than épaule width. The bar should be resting on top of your cuisses. vos bras should be extended with a slight bend at the coudes and votre dos should be straight. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Use your side épaules to lift the cable bar as you expirez. The bar should be close to the body as you move it up. Continue to lift it until it nearly touches your chin. Conseil : Your coudes should drive the motion. As you lift the bar, your coudes should always be higher than your forearms. Also, keep your torse stationary and pause for a second at the top of le mouvement.
3. Lower the bar back down Lentement, to the position de départ. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Upright_Cable_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Upright Row - With Bands', 'Trapèzes', 'Élastique', '1. To begin, stand on an exercise band so that tension begins at arm''s length. Grasp the handles using a pronated (paumes vers your cuisses) grip that is slightly less than épaule width. The handles should be resting on top of your cuisses. vos bras should be extended with a slight bend at the coudes and votre dos should be straight. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Use your side épaules to lift the handles as you expirez. The handles should be close to the body as you move them up. Continue to lift the handles until they nearly touches your chin. Conseil : Your coudes should drive the motion. As you lift the handles, your coudes should always be higher than your forearms. Also, keep your torse stationary and pause for a second at the top of le mouvement.
3. Lower the handles back down Lentement, to the position de départ. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Upright_Row_-_With_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Upward Stretch', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. Extend both hands straight above votre tête, palms touching.
2. Lentement, push vos mains up and back, keeping votre dos straight.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Upward_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('V-Bar Pulldown', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Sit down on a pull-down machine with a V-Bar attached to the top pulley.
2. Adjust the genou pad of the machine to fit your height. These pads will prevent votre corps from being raised by the resistance attached to the bar.
3. Grab the V-bar with the paumes vers each other (a neutral grip). Stick your poitrine out and lean yourself back slightly (around 30-degrees) in order to better engage the lats. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Using your lats, pull the bar down as you squeeze your omoplates. Continue until your poitrine nearly touches the V-bar. Expirez as you execute this motion. Conseil : Keep the torse stationary throughout le mouvement.
5. After a second hold on the contracted position, Lentement, bring the bar back to the position de départ as you Inspirez.
6. Répétez for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/V-Bar_Pulldown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('V-Bar Pullup', 'Dos', 'Poids de corps', '1. Start by placing the middle of the V-bar in the middle of the pull-up bar (assuming that the pull-up station you are using does not have neutral grip handles). The V-Bar handles will be facing down so that you can hang from the pull-up bar through the use of the handles.
2. Once you securely place the V-bar, take a hold of the bar from each side and hang from it. Stick your poitrine out and lean yourself back slightly in order to better engage the lats. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Using your lats, pull your torse up while leaning votre tête back slightly so that you do not hit yourself with the chin-up bar. Continue until your poitrine nearly touches the V-bar. Expirez as you execute this motion.
4. After a second hold on the contracted position, Lentement, lower votre corps back to the position de départ as you Inspirez.
5. Répétez for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/V-Bar_Pullup/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Vertical Swing', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Haltères', '1. Allow the haltère to hang bras tendus between vos jambes, holding it with both hands. Keep votre dos straight and votre tête up.
2. Swing the haltère between vos jambes, flexing at the hanches and bending the genous slightly.
3. Powerfully reverse the motion by extending at the hanches, genous, and chevilles to propel yourself upward, swinging the dumbell over votre tête.
4. As you land, absorb the impact through vos jambes and draw the haltère to your torse before the next repetition.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Quadriceps, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Vertical_Swing/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Walking, Treadmill', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, step onto the treadmill and select the desired option from the menu. Most treadmills have a manual setting, or you can select a program to run. Typically, you can enter your age and poids to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise. Elevation can be adjusted to change the intensity of the workout.
2. Treadmills offer convenience, cardiovascular benefits, and usually have less impact than walking outside. When walking, you should move at a moderate to fast pace, not a leisurely one. Being an activity of lower intensity, walking doesn''t burn as many calories as some other activities, but still provides great benefit. A 150 lb person will burn about 175 calories walking 4 miles per hour for 30 minutes, compared to 450 calories running twice as fast. Maintain proper posture as you walk, and only hold onto the handles when necessary, such as when dismounting or checking your heart rate.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Walking_Treadmill/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
